    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d230">

                <pb facs="0395" n="1853" sameAs="frus:frus1951v07p2/pg1853"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">601.84A93/11–2151: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the Embassy in France
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1951-11-21T19:11:00-05:00">November 21,
                            1951—7:11 p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3100. Since appears Sharett intended invite our comment by informing Secy in
                    confidence re possible estab Israel Leg Peiping and particularly since Sharett
                    implies some US official encouragement this proposed step, we believe it
                    important Secy inform him<anchor n="1" xml:id="d230-f1"/> that, far from
                    encouraging such move, we for our part believe it wld be most inappropriate at
                    time when Chinese Communists engaged active hostilities against UN for any UN
                    member to recognize Communist China or, if recognition already extended, to
                    proceed estab Leg and exchange reps. Furthermore, such action might run counter
                    to spirit GA Res <pb facs="0396" n="1854"
                        xml:id="pg1854"/> Feb 1 finding Communist China an aggressor and calling on
                    all states and auths to refrain from giving any assistance to aggressor in
                    Korea. Estab Leg in Peiping by Israel this time might be considered as moral
                    support for Communist regime and as such cld be construed as assistance.</p>
                <p>
                    FYI Dept unable identify “stateside official
                    quarters” and doubts any US official encouraged Sharett as intimated.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Webb</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d230-f1" n="1" xml:id="d230-f1-content">
                <p>Secretary Acheson left Paris on the morning of November 23; telegram Delga 355 from Paris, November 24, stated that
                    Plitt would call on Sharett to convey the substance of the Department’s message
                    (320/11–2451).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
